From: Dhaval Gujar <dhaval.gujar@espressif.com>
Subject: [PATCH] esp32s31: reset the whole system on SBI reboot

The SBI system-reset handler triggered only the HP core 0 software reset
(LP_AONCLKRST_HPCORE0_RESET_CTRL_REG bit 20). On an ESP32-S31 running
Linux, "reboot" then stops after "reboot: Restarting system" and the board
never boots again until EN is pulsed. Use the digital-system software reset
(LP_SYSTEM_REG_SYS_CTRL_REG.SYS_SW_RST) that the ROM's software_reset()
uses instead.

Upstream: not yet submitted

--- a/platform/generic/espressif/esp32s31/esp32s31.c
+++ b/platform/generic/espressif/esp32s31/esp32s31.c
@@ -51,11 +51,13 @@
 /* Slack over the source dtb for the generic platform's in-place fixups. */
 #define S31_FIXUP_FDT_SIZE	0x3000
 
-/* LP_AONCLKRST_HPCORE0_RESET_CTRL_REG @ 0x2070103C — bit 20 is the
- * write-to-trigger HP core 0 software reset, used to service SBI
- * shutdown / reboot requests. */
-#define LP_AONCLKRST_HPCORE0_RESET_CTRL_REG  0x2070103CU
-#define HPCORE_SW_RESET                      (1U << 20)
+/* LP_SYSTEM_REG_SYS_CTRL_REG @ 0x20700008 — bit 1 (SYS_SW_RST) resets the
+ * whole digital system, as the ROM's software_reset() does, used to service
+ * SBI shutdown / reboot requests. Resetting HP core 0 alone is not enough:
+ * the clocks, MSPI and caches Linux left configured survive it and the ROM
+ * never boots again. */
+#define LP_SYSTEM_REG_SYS_CTRL_REG           0x20700008U
+#define LP_SYSTEM_REG_SYS_SW_RST             (1U << 1)
 
 static int s31_system_reset_check(u32 type, u32 reason)
 {
@@ -70,7 +72,9 @@
 
 static void s31_system_reset(u32 type, u32 reason)
 {
-	writel(HPCORE_SW_RESET, (void *)LP_AONCLKRST_HPCORE0_RESET_CTRL_REG);
+	void *sys_ctrl = (void *)LP_SYSTEM_REG_SYS_CTRL_REG;
+
+	writel(readl(sys_ctrl) | LP_SYSTEM_REG_SYS_SW_RST, sys_ctrl);
 
 	/* If the reset doesn't take effect (e.g. shutdown on a chip with no
 	 * power-down path), spin in WFI so we don't return into garbage. */
